    "checks": [
      "An accessory apartment is permitted by right in R-1, R-3, R-4, CV, CRV, A and V (27-401). Blank cells in the table mean not permitted, and the listed uses are the only uses (27-303)",
      "The apartment must be part of the principal structure: added onto or created within a single-family dwelling, with its own kitchen, bathroom and sleeping area. One per lot (27-202, 27-602)",
      "'Apartments or other living quarters shall not be permitted in an accessory structure/building, except as provided for in Part 6' (27-502.1.G)",
      "Parking: 'The required two parking spaces per dwelling must be provided' (27-602.1)",
      "A separate 'accessory family dwelling unit' is also permitted by right in the same districts. It is for the owner's relatives with a medical hardship, at most two persons, never rented, renewed every year, and may be a detached portable unit up to 900 sq ft and 15 ft high in the side or rear yard (27-202, 27-603)",
      "No owner-occupancy or size rule is set for the accessory apartment",
      "District density limits (R-1 one unit per half acre in the growth area, R-3 five and R-4 eight units per acre) may count the apartment. Not settled",
      "A two-family dwelling is permitted in R-3 and R-4, and a residential conversion by special exception in R-3"
    ],
    "notes": "Zoning office: Dover Township, York County (dovertownship.org). Read in a browser on American Legal (codelibrary.amlegal.com/codes/dovertwp), one page at a time. Use table 27-401 read from the screen to place each P in its column. District rules read for CV, A, V, R-1, R-3, R-4 and the Crossroads Village (CRV) overlay. Part 6 standards other than 27-602 and 27-603 and Part 7 parking were not read."
